  "text": "“Hydrogen Blending Impacts Study” suggests that below 5% may be OK (https://docs.cpuc.ca.gov/PublishedDocs/Efile/G000/M493/K760/493760600.PDF [3]). It should be noted that all ASPEN Plus process models were fitted to match lab-scale data provided by West Biofuels. All inputs provided by West Biofuels were used verbatim with respect to inlet, recycle, and product compositions and flow rates which in some cases required forced application of correction factors to the otherwise calculated ASPEN model outputs. Consequently, given the scale of the provided data and model uncertainties, care should be taken in extrapolating these results to a commercial-scale system. 7 This report is available at no cost from the National Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR) at www.nrel.gov/publications. Table of Contents Executive Summary ..................................................................................................................................... 6 1 Introduction .......................................................................................................................................... 10 2 Design Basis ........................................................................................................................................ 10 2.1 Experimental West Biofuels Data ................................................................................................ 11 2.1.1 High Alcohols Case ........................................................................................................ 11 2.1.2 High Renewable Gas Case .............................................................................................. 13 2.2 Aspen Plus Model Details ............................................................................................................ 16 3 Process Design and Key Assumptions ............................................................................................ 16 3.1 Area 100: Feed Handling and Drying .......